{"type":"text","timestamp":1794310114331,"sessionID":"ses_e3acfc49dffeH5YsYOrtrLU303","part":{"id":"prt_1c537462a001qGct3ZjptfQYVd","sessionID":"ses_e3acfc49dffeH5YsYOrtrLU303","messageID":"msg_1c5370fc80011AR4yexSJmPbMi","type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass. Here's what I did:\n\n1. **Created `clients/retry.py`** — `call_with_retry(fn, sleep, attempts=3, base_delay=0.1)` loops up to `attempts` times, calls `fn()`, and only retries on `TransientError` with exponential backoff. Other exceptions propagate immediately; no sleep after the final attempt.\n\n2. **Refactored `clients/orders.py`** — Both `get_order` and `cancel_order` now delegate to `call_with_retry`, removing their duplicate retry loops.\n\n3. **Refactored `clients/users.py`** — `get_user` now uses `call_with_retry`, fixing the bug where it retried *all* exceptions (including `PermanentError`) and always slept even after the last attempt.","time":{"start":1794310096426,"end":1794310114331}}}
